      "fondo": "monte",
      "camara": {
        "de": 0,
        "a": 900
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "en": "They came down from the temple and threw stones over their shoulders, without looking back.",
          "es": "Bajaron del templo y arrojaron piedras por encima del hombro, sin mirar atrás."
        },
        {
          "en": "The stones softened and took shape, like statues beginning to be carved.",
          "es": "Las piedras se ablandaron y tomaron forma, como estatuas que empiezan a tallarse."
        },
        {
          "en": "The stones Deucalion threw became men. The stones Pyrrha threw became women.",
          "es": "Las piedras que lanzó Deucalión se volvieron hombres. Las que lanzó Pirra se volvieron mujeres."
        },
        {
          "en": "That is why humans are a hardy race, able to endure toil and pain.",
          "es": "Por eso los humanos son una raza dura, capaz de soportar el trabajo y el dolor."
        },
        {
          "en": "Deucalion and Pyrrha also had a son, Hellen. The Greeks were later called Hellenes, from his name.",
          "es": "Deucalión y Pirra también tuvieron un hijo, Helén. Más tarde los griegos fueron llamados helenos, por su nombre."
        }
      ],
